From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:43:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dxvk: drain pending frees before a heap passes its budget,
 and fail an allocation rather than hand out no storage

The Witcher 3 1.32 on the forced 8 GB row (V 2,048 MiB) crashed 8 s
after its first frame: its render thread read address 0x78 in
DxvkImage::assignStorageWithUsage, called from the DxvkImage
constructor. In about a second the game's render targets had grown
from 155 to 994 MiB, 642 MiB more were released but held by GPU work
in flight, and Metal refused new heaps once the driver held about
2.1 GiB. createImageResource logged "Memory allocation failed" and
returned no storage, which the constructor, like every caller of an
allocation that must succeed, dereferenced. DXVK 2.4 threw a DxvkError
there, which a resource's creation reports as an error.

On a unified memory device DXVK never enforces a heap's budget, and it
never waits for the memory GPU work in flight holds: the storage a
discard retired and the storage of a released resource come back only
when the command list that used them last completes. Now an allocation
that must succeed (not a relocation or eviction, which pass NoFallback,
NoAllocation or NoDeviceMemory) is first tried with the new
WithinBudget mode, which allocates no device memory that would take
its heap past the budget. Failing that, it waits for the submissions in
flight until they have freed as much as it needs or none is left, then
is tried as asked, and may grow past the budget. If that fails too it
throws "DxvkMemoryAllocator: Memory allocation failed", and a buffer or
image whose storage it was unregisters itself before the exception
leaves its constructor. A drain that waited logs, at most once a
second:

  [dxvk-drain] waited W ms, F MiB freed for N MiB | drains=D waited=T ms freed=M MiB

The policy and its counters are in dxvk_memory_drain.h, which makes no
Vulkan call.

Linear: PLA-875
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: tools/tests/test_dxvk_memory_drain.py (host); the phone run (The Witcher 3 1.32 past first frame +300 s on the forced 8 GB row) is PLA-875's check, not run here
Offered-upstream: no
